course: dictionary
lesson: 9997
title: Teething and teething problems
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Teethe is a verb. When a baby teethes, its first teeth push up through the gums. Context helps you understand it: a baby who is teething can be sore, grumpy and dribbly.
explain: Read «The first baby tooth usually comes through at about six months, often at the bottom front, and teething can make a baby grumpy and dribbly.» The words grumpy and dribbly are clues. Teething makes babies uncomfortable, so teethe is about a baby's first teeth coming through.
explain: Teething is also used in the phrase «teething problems». Here it is not about a baby at all. It means small faults that appear when something new is starting, like a new school or a new computer system.
fact: Teethe means that a baby's first teeth are growing through the gums.
fact: Teethe is a verb: teethes, teethed, teething.
fact: A baby who is teething can be sore, grumpy and dribbly.
fact: A «teething ring» is a toy that a baby can chew on while teething.
fact: «Teething problems» means small faults in something new.
exercise: «The baby is teething, so she is grumpy and dribbly.» What does teething mean? | She has just had a bath | *Her first teeth are growing through her gums | She is learning to walk | Her last teeth are falling out
exercise: «The first baby tooth usually comes through at about six months, often at the bottom front.» Where do the first teeth usually come through? | At the top back | At about two years old | *At the bottom front | In the middle of the back
exercise: Ella says, «The new school's teething problems are nearly over.» What does teething problems mean here? | *Small faults when something new is starting | Pain in the mouth from a new tooth | Problems caused by the dentist | A school just for babies
test: «Mum gave the baby a cold teething ring to chew.» What is a teething ring for? | To keep the baby warm | To wear on a finger | *To chew on | To make a noise
test: «Yesterday the baby ___ badly, so Dad fetched the cold spoon.» Choose the correct form of teethe. | teethes | teething | teethe | *teethed
exam: «The new computer system had teething troubles at first, but now it works well.» What does teething troubles mean? | Problems at the dentist | Broken parts that cannot be fixed | A sore mouth from new teeth | *Small faults when something is new
